1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,120
Payment blocked.

2
00:00:02,400 --> 00:00:05,800
Leadership had an answer:
“We added a RACI.”

3
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:09,500
Four roles.
One clean diagram.

4
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:17,600
The agent follows the “A.”

5
00:00:19,450 --> 00:00:24,800
“I own the supplier relationship.
I don’t own payment release.”

6
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:32,500
Finance owns the control. Operations sees the supply risk.
Accounts Payable can stop the invoice.

7
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:37,100
Everyone has a letter.
No one has the decision.

8
00:00:38,200 --> 00:00:43,400
The missing artifact isn’t another role map.
It’s a decision contract.

9
00:00:45,600 --> 00:00:53,300
Try this with one real exception. Ask two experienced people:
who decides, who acts, within what limit, using what evidence?

10
00:00:53,300 --> 00:00:58,900
Compare their answers. Where they disagree,
you found hidden organization design.

11
00:00:58,900 --> 00:01:02,400
Make it explicit
before the agent executes.
